"id": "adverbs",
"el": "Τα επιρρήματα",
"title": "Adverbs",
"span": "A1–B2",
"blurb": "Adverbs from adjectives in -α and -ως, the everyday adverbs of place, time, frequency and degree, and the pairs that trip learners up: ακόμα and πια, απλά and απλώς, καθόλου.",
"intro": [
{
"p": "Adverbs never change their form. Most of them are made from adjectives, and the rule is simple: take the **neuter plural** of the adjective. **Καλός → καλά** \"well\", **γρήγορος → γρήγορα** \"quickly\", **ωραίος → ωραία** \"nicely\"."
},
{
"p": "A second set, from older Greek, ends in **-ως**: **ακριβώς** \"exactly\", **ευτυχώς** \"luckily\", **συνήθως** \"usually\". The rest are short everyday words for place and time (**εδώ, εκεί, τώρα, μετά**) that you simply learn."
},
